10. Important Notes
•	The program validates the number mathematically; it does not contact a bank or payment network.
•	The accepted prefixes are determined by the conditions written in the program.
•	The current implementation stores the card number in a long long variable.
•	For production software, a card number is generally better treated as text so that leading zeros can be preserved.
•	The <string> header is included in the source code but is not currently required by the implementation.
11. Conclusion
This project demonstrates the use of C++ functions, conditional statements, loops, arithmetic operators, modulus, integer division, and function decomposition. It also demonstrates how the Luhn algorithm can be implemented to perform a basic credit card number validation.
